<title>USA: N.J. governor says to sign port dredging bill.</title>
<headline>N.J. governor says to sign port dredging bill.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-05-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>New Jersey Gov. Christine Whitman said Wednesday she would sign legislation on Thursday to implement a voter-approved $230 million bond plan for dredging state ports and waterways.</p>
<p>The money will be used to deepen the channels in Newark Bay and the port region, and to help pay to dispose of the dredged silt, sand and mud.</p>
<p>The governor said she would also tour a cargo ship at Port Newark after signing the bill.</p>
<p>--Steven Dickson, 212-859-1652</p>
</text>
